WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.370
The Age of Gods was closing.
Eternity had come to an end.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:33.950
The clash between the armies of Falis,
God of Light, and Falaris, God of Darkness,

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.450
split the heavens in two.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:52.060
In the unceasing battle which
followed, the earth wept.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.170
The seas boiled.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.720
At last, only two survivors
remained on both sides.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.600
Marfa, Goddess of Creation, and
Kardis, Goddess of Destruction...

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.970
who met in a clash which
echoed to the ends of the earth.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.730
At the end of
the fierce battle...

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.110
a new land was born,
split off from the continent.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.880
And the life's fires of the
goddesses of Light and Dark...

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.130
flickered and died away.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.580
Thousands of years
have since passed.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.270
And now, the land to the south
of the continent of Alecrast...

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:03.150
has become known as
"Lodoss - The Accursed Island."

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.490
So, this is the Dwarves'
Great Tunnel, huh?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:21.450
They say you could buy dwarf
goods here for a good price.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:26.230
It must have been home to
many skilled dwarf craftsmen.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:35.300
That was a long time ago.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:41.800
Hey, you sure we gotta go through
here to get to Wort's place?

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:47.460
There are safer paths to take,
but we haven't the time.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.280
It smells so moldy in here!

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.900
You don't like it,
then stay behind!

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.090
Better that than having an elf
befouling my ancestors' home!

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.710
I beg your pardon?!

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.220
Ghim! Deedlit!
Both of you, stop it!

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:04.370
If we don't get to Wort soon,
all of Lodoss could be in danger!

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.730
I know, but!

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.040
I'm only doing this
because I want to.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.740
Nobody's forcing
you to tag along!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.200
Excuse me?!

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.700
This isn't the place for
you both to be arguing!

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.000
Wood!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.510
Get inside!
We're sitting ducks out here!

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.880
Right, move it!

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.140
...who have been
hardened by the gods.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.860
Throw off these false garments
and reveal your true forms.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:27.780
Creators of all things,
shield us from this evil...

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.550
Whatta waste. We'd get a good
price for this if it was finished.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.760
Oh, it's beautiful!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.110
Hey, what do you think?

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.620
We're not here for that.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.620
It suits you. Really!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.570
Thanks.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.340
Who's there?!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:22.580
Some evil presence is
interfering with our journey.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:00.790
None may escape time's march,
or so they say...

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:11.380
Has it really been so long...

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.210
since the battle in the
labyrinth's depths?

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.670
Who are you?

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:28.700
Was it not you who
vowed to protect me...

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:31.810
before you charged
that demon? My dear Wort.

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.810
Ah yes, the memories
surface within you.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:40.410
Of your companions,
the Six Heroes.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.820
But?!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:43.740
What is a body?

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:48.330
A mere dress, to be worn or
discarded with the ages.

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:02.470
How much further
does it go?

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.350
We'll just have to trust Ghim's
intuition while we're in here.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:10.250
What'd you expect?! The size of
the Great Tunnel is legendary!

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:14.290
Just get us out! I don't fancy
losing my head down here!

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.610
Relax, lad. This isn't
a maze we're wandering.

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.520
If we keep moving forward,
we'll find the way out.

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:26.240
Takes a long time when the
dwarf's leading, doesn't it?

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.250
This place is really
giving me the creeps.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.790
No! Leave it be!

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:48.730
Deed!

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:50.800
Let go!

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:51.890
My hand!

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.110
Parn!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.140
Bloody hell!

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:58.870
Deed!

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:36.710
You're going to seek
out the sage, Wort?

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:37.650
Yes, majesty.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.880
Kannon and Alania have already
fallen to the Marmo forces.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:46.070
The only remaining regular
troops are those here in Valis.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.320
Wort may tell you
what you seek to learn...

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:51.720
but there is no guarantee
you'll make it back safely.

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:54.790
I know, majesty. But only
the sage can tell us...

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.390
what we need to know
about that witch, Karla.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.020
That armor?!

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:09.010
A legacy of my father,
a former retainer of yours.

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:21.090
King Fahn.

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.350
King Kashue.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:32.120
I like that boy, Parn.
Good eyes on him.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:39.010
I never thought I'd meet
the son of Tessius.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:42.260
No. Deep down,
I knew I would.

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.650
Tessius?!

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:53.810
I have never so cursed
my position as I did that time.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:14:00.710
Parn.
Come through this safely.

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.200
So, where are we?

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:15.670
It would seem we've been invited
into a secret hall of sorts.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.290
What's that?

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.870
Oh, don't you know?

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:31.910
Look!

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:40.420
Anyway, we'd better get out
of here and rejoin the others.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.590
What's wrong?

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:46.920
Take a look at this.

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.570
It's...

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:55.100
Some sort of mural,
I think.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:56.080
Hold on.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:02.340
Spirit of light, mother that
nourishes plants, come unto me.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:15.560
What the?

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.560
I've heard about
this story.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:21.820
The time of the
final battle had come.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.870
Falaris, God of Darkness, led an
army of 1000 ancient dragons...

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:30.610
and evil gods
against Falis, the Supreme.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.370
It was a vicious battle,
Falis and his forces of Light...

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.350
against Falaris' army of Darkness.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:40.550
The gods were finally destroyed
by their own great power.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:50.040
It's a very old legend.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:53.010
They were destroyed
by their own power?

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.060
I suppose it means they grew
too powerful for their own good.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:59.640
If they were that powerful, a war
wasn't really necessary, was it?

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:04.650
That's a strange thing for
a would-be hero to say, Parn.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:07.160
Uh, well...
I just meant...

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.050
I don't understand
you humans at all.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:12.000
But then, I suppose that's
what makes you so fascinating.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.580
To my staff I call the power
to turn back the darkness.

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.730
Handy little thing
to have around.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.660
Come on!
We have to save Parn!

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:34.040
Don't worry,
the elf girl's with him.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:40.140
The air currents will show
her the way out, sure enough.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.250
Can't figure it.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:45.430
You and Deed are always at each other's
throats, but now you compliment her!

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.540
Shut yer hole!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:52.150
Only a human would let his feelings
keep him from recognizing someone's skills!

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:56.740
Sylph, spirit of wind.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.960
Let thy currents
guide us to the surface.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.840
Sylph, spirit of wind.

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:08.960
Let thy currents
guide us to the surface.

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:20.880
Thank you, Sylph.

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:27.080
You, once of the Six Heroes,
now feared as the Gray Witch.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.510
What are you up to now?!

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:33.620
Are you aware of the dragon
who hates being awakened...

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.490
who lives near the
exit of the Great Tunnel?

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.900
What is it, Deed?

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:08.230
Hey, what's the hold-up?!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.190
Is something wrong, Slayn?

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:27.350
Deed!

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:29.570
Shh! Not a sound!

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:46.900
I'll lead him off.
You break for that passage.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.850
Don't be ridiculous!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.870
Deed, what's
its weak point?!

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.940
How am I supposed to know?!

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:37.030
Damn!

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:52.960
Slayn!

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:56.950
Are they alright?!

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:58.380
Oh, for the love of!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.750
Slayn!

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:15.780
You alright?

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.030
Hell! That thing's
gonna eat us!

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:23.030
Then we'll just have
to eat him first!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.300
Parn's in over his head!
Ghim, what are you waiting for?!

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:40.420
Silence, elf!
A dwarf fights by his own lore!

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.880
Parn!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:13.420
Ghim!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:29.010
Now!

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:40.230
Now's our chance!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.000
The exit! We made it!

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:05.010
The obstacle is cleared,
as I said it would be. Now then...

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:11.010
Let us wait. That is why
I have come, after all.

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:14.220
As you wish.
It's no concern of mine.

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:16.520
All of Lodoss is trembling.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:23.450
That fate will balance
the scales of history...

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:27.100
is all that I desire.

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:35.600
The heroes' journey
has only just begun.

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:40.670
And before them lies
an unimaginable destiny.

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:57.710
The cursed island of
Lodoss faces a great evil.

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:00.560
Creatures attack our people,
and set our villages afire.

00:23:00.750 --> 00:23:03.500
Two friends are reunited,
and an encounter with a new one...

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:05.440
leads a young man
to embark on a journey.

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:10.580
Next time,
on Record of Lodoss War:

00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:13.010
Episode 2 - "Blazing Departure"

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:15.110
I will defend the peace
of Lodoss with my life!
